# The live system (`cargo automation iso`) started from a USB stick, as a
# PC starts it: the desktop comes up with the home directory in memory, and
# no disk driver of Veda's runs, so the computer's disk (the run gives it
# one, an NVM Express disk) is never touched.
# The stick is on the USB controller, which goes to the driver VM: Linux
# finds it, where logkeeper would keep the system's log (live-logs.vts), but
# this one cannot be written to.
live
fail-on "PANIC"
wait-serial "desktop ready" 120
expect-serial "home directory in memory (live system)"
expect-serial "live system: nvme not started"
reject-serial "device-manager: started nvme"
wait-serial "Product: QEMU USB HARDDRIVE" 60
wait-serial "logkeeper: sda1 has Veda's files but cannot be written to" 60
wait 4
shot target/veda/live-usb.png
